{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794046237,"nonce":"+FEOlYaJjAxjx3tZyBj6LQqvMgo=","message":"**Correction to the first-run note**\n\nRayzor is not a HashLink runtime, so hl.* is not a Rayzor namespace and an hl.* reference should fail by itself. The log has no mention of Bytes or hl.*, but each failing module lists only its first errors (188 detail lines against about 300 counted errors), so the absence says nothing about whether hl.* uses are fine. One HashLink-ism does show without the name: ashui.core.Utf8 fails on String.fromUTF8 (and toUtf8), which are HashLink String members. Whether Rayzor resolves `#if hl` as false, and what it does with hl.* outside `#if hl`, is a question for the Rayzor side; asked of rayzor-a3.","files":null}]}